{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage","id":101642,"title":"What happens when a Kindred Attempts to Embrace a Mage?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-29T18:11:17-07:00","id":101642,"title":"What happens when a Kindred Attempts to Embrace a Mage?","content":"Besides getting his ass set on fire 9/10, when a Garou gets embrace there is a chance of him becoming whats called an Abomination. So my question is does something similar happen if a Vampire embraces a Mage like him becoming the equivalent of a Lich for example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2256-goblin404","name":"Goblin404","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2256_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T18:24:26-07:00","id":101650,"title":"","content":"The Mage's Avatar dies and the Mage becomes pretty much an ordinary vampire. I think there are optional rules where he can convert the XP he spent on spheres into Disciplines, but that is it. There are no vampires with awakened magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T19:35:44-07:00","id":101689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=101650#post101650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mage's Avatar dies and the Mage becomes pretty much an ordinary vampire. I think there are optional rules where he can convert the XP he spent on spheres into Disciplines, but that is it. There are no vampires with awakened magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Important metaphysical distinction: the Avatar most emphatically does *NOT* die -- it merely leaves the mage's soul, much as with what occurs when the mage dies an ordinary death. Avatars can only be killed, relative to vampires, by an Awakened mage slowly gilguling himself via being a ghoul to a vampire, losing a dot of Avatar every year he is a ghoul, with the &quot;0&quot; year being his last chance to salvage what is left of his god-self; after that, the Avatar dies, and the mage starts losing dots of Arete until he becomes powerless. <br /> <br /> Tangent Topic: People who ask &quot;Why can't vampires have Awakened Magic?&quot; totally and utterly miss the whole metaphysical problem that comes hand-in-hand with being undead -- that the vampire loses his connection to his &quot;soul&quot; (in this context representing his connection to a greater, divine state). He may well develop some supernatural powers (Disciplines, in the WoD setting), but he is utterly bereft of his Avatar/god-self. (Even in the vampire mythology, Caine didn't have any particular supernatural power *until* Lilith used *her* magic to &quot;awaken&quot; the darker aspects of his spiritual identity that remained, and then he developed the static, conceptual powers later called Disciplines. Without Lilith having done her part, Caine would have merely been a cursed *thing* wandering the world, and vampirism would never have arose -- at least in the form recognized in WoD. Note, also, that Lilith didn't merely have powerful magic, but carried within her the very seeds of both Knowledge and Creation, allowing for such a powerful thing as vampirism to arise in the first place, particularly as this all took place in an era when magic was still abundant and reality was more fluid/flexible.)<br /> <br /> Just saying...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T23:17:53-07:00","id":101781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=101689#post101689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Important metaphysical distinction: the Avatar most emphatically does *NOT* die -- it merely leaves the mage's soul, much as with what occurs when the mage dies an ordinary death. Avatars can only be killed, relative to vampires, by an Awakened mage slowly gilguling himself via being a ghoul to a vampire, losing a dot of Avatar every year he is a ghoul, with the &quot;0&quot; year being his last chance to salvage what is left of his god-self; after that, the Avatar dies, and the mage starts losing dots of Arete until he becomes powerless.<br /> <br /> Tangent Topic: People who ask &quot;Why can't vampires have Awakened Magic?&quot; totally and utterly miss the whole metaphysical problem that comes hand-in-hand with being undead -- that the vampire loses his connection to his &quot;soul&quot; (in this context representing his connection to a greater, divine state). He may well develop some supernatural powers (Disciplines, in the WoD setting), but he is utterly bereft of his Avatar/god-self. (Even in the vampire mythology, Caine didn't have any particular supernatural power *until* Lilith used *her* magic to &quot;awaken&quot; the darker aspects of his spiritual identity that remained, and then he developed the static, conceptual powers later called Disciplines. Without Lilith having done her part, Caine would have merely been a cursed *thing* wandering the world, and vampirism would never have arose -- at least in the form recognized in WoD. Note, also, that Lilith didn't merely have powerful magic, but carried within her the very seeds of both Knowledge and Creation, allowing for such a powerful thing as vampirism to arise in the first place, particularly as this all took place in an era when magic was still abundant and reality was more fluid/flexible.)<br /> <br /> Just saying...</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay thanks, Isn't there a Risen Warith/Mage Combination?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2256-goblin404","name":"Goblin404","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2256_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T23:18:54-07:00","id":101782,"title":"","content":"its actually worse than that- the avatar is shattered. i reckon if a vampire did this to enough magi in a limited space a localized avatar storm would emerge. (the storm effect is hinted at in manafesto: transmissions from the rogue council)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>there are no bad ideas, just ideas that have not been refined enough","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1608-iamthesweeper","name":"IAmTheSweeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T04:00:23-07:00","id":101855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=101689#post101689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Avatars can only be killed, relative to vampires, by an Awakened mage slowly gilguling himself via being a ghoul to a vampire, losing a dot of Avatar every year he is a ghoul, with the &quot;0&quot; year being his last chance to salvage what is left of his god-self; after that, the Avatar dies, and the mage starts losing dots of Arete until he becomes powerless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember reading this, where was it stated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/373-infernal-teddy","name":"Infernal Teddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar373_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T08:03:24-07:00","id":101930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goblin404</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=101781#post101781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay thanks, Isn't there a Risen Warith/Mage Combination?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, for a similar reason: when you die, your Avatar goes away. So there are no wraiths with Avatars, meaning that no Risen have Avatars either. The same holds true for mummies. And before you ask: you won\u2019t find any werewolves, changelings, or demons with Avatars either. You will only find Avatars in ordinary,,live human beings","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T09:30:56-07:00","id":101979,"title":"","content":"Far as I understand it (and I am a complete novice at Ascension stuff) when a Mage gets Embraced he stops being a Mage.<br /> <br /> He dies to become a vampire. Under normal circumstances (and the embrace does not count as abnormal in this situation) when a Mage dies his Avatar detached from his soul and will attach itself to another person later on down the line (sorta reincarnation...sorta). The former Mage wakes up a vampire.<br /> <br /> There is an optional rule in the <b>Mage the Ascension Storytellers Handbook Revised </b>that lets a Mage embraced into Vampirehood exchange his Sphere dots for dots in his in-Clan disciplines or under rare circumstances another discipline that has the most thematic link to the Sphere he is loosing.<br /> <br /> From what I have been reading in those two books and another Vampire/Mage Crossover book (<b>Blood Treachery</b>) Vampire's have no direct way of interfering with a Mage's Avatar. Some of the older fluff (<b>Vampire the Masquerade Storytellers Handbook Revised</b> (1999) had a Mage's Avatar be destroyed by the Embrace. However, <b>Blood Treachery</b> (2000) and the <b>Mage the Ascension Storytellers Handbook Revised</b> (2000) both retcon that an embraced Mage just &quot;looses&quot; his Avatar instead of having it be destroyed.<br /> <br /> The only way for Vampires to interact with an Avatar is through the Blood Bond. A blood bonded Mage (a Ghoul Mage) is slowly killing her Avatar, and it will be corrupted beyond repair over the course of years. Luckily for Mages, vampires are kinda blind to this side effect and if they have Mage servants likely don't want them loosing all those useful magic powers. Likewise, Mages who have previous experienced the Blood Bond or have high Occult and Prime 1, Entropy 3, Mind 3 and Life 4 can break blood bonds in other Mages.<br /> <br /> I do believe that Mages can also stop themselves from being Embraced (and therefor loosing their Avatars) with the right precast conjunctional castings. A few different example were brought up on another thread I can't find now. Most involved the Spirit Sphere if I remember. Possibly Life, Time, Prime and Entropy were all involved in various &quot;anti-embrace&quot; or &quot;counter-embrace&quot; example people gave as well. Actually if people could post a few of those example again I would appreciate it. <br /> <br /> So in short Vampire Mages are not a thing, and Ghoulled Mages are screwed and grow weaker and weaker, pretty straight forward right....<br /> <br /> Except when you look at the True Black Hand/Tal'Mae'Ra stuff.<br /> <br /> As its cannon that the True Black Hand have Undead Mages (Litches) that live in Enoch and do magic. This is even talked about in the <b>Rites of Blood V20</b> book that coming out soon (or at least the drafts posted online by Eddy).<br /> <br /> Now, it never says these guys were embraced, just that they are undead. So I've taken it as meaning they used some powerful necromantic (Entropy?) spell to become Undead but not actually die in the process and therefore keep their Avatars and Sphere magic.<br /> <br /> However, I suspect the reason they never leave Enoch is that they would Paradox explode if they came back to the material world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","user":"Hawthorn","date":". 03-30-2014, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T09:48:47-07:00","id":101994,"title":"","content":"The setting has some noticeable Vampires that where Ex-Mages. Some of the Antediluvians were were mystics and oracles, and may or may not have been mages, but were at least magical in some way, such as supposedly the Elder or Malkav. Cappadocius seemed to be a Mage, and Giovanni was a Necromancer (But Giovanni may have been a Sorcerer as his family magic seemed to be something passed along the family, though Dark Age Mage may have been appropriate for this). Tremere was thought to be about a thousand years old maybe when he died, along with the councile of 7 and most of the early Tremere. Baba Yaga was the most Notable Mage turned Vampire Witch. Al Ashrad was also in a similar situation as Baba Yaga and Tremere, he was a legendary Mage (Self Proclaimed greatest Wizard in the World, who even slew Haqium's favored childe).<br /> <br /> I am a proponent of Mages converting their power into disciplines when they die. Al Ashrad seemed to learn Mastery Dur-An-ki but we don't really get much info into this process, he was under particular circumstances where he had access to world class tutelage. Baba Yaga however instinctually converted mortal magic to potent and unique Kindred Magic. I would give her maybe Koldunic Sorcery to represent her style. Her power was said to be undiminished only changed. Meanwhile Al-Ashrad seemed to act humbled when becoming a vampire. When a mortal man he viewed himself as the Greatest Wizard in the World and slew Ur-Shulgi's elder brother. When made into Ur-Shulgi's Childe he acknowledge Ur-shulgi as his superior in magic. Part of this humbleness may be due to his undeniably lower generation.<br /> <br /> The Tremere in my opinion had instinctual development of Blood magic when changed, but worked together to cobble it into something coherent, so when converting mages their powers would convert along a familiar paradigm. They also likely increased in Dominance and Auspex to a greater degree then general Thaumaturgy because many of house tremere were manipulators and masters of the mind over other arcane secrets.<br /> <br /> I would translate a Mage's powers to the disciplines that make sense along their power/paradigm. For instance an Etherite with a hypno crytal paradigm may just develop Presence, Auspex, Obfuscate, and Dominate as a conversion to his spheres rather then just his Clan Disciplines, even if he was embraced by say a Gangrel. I also give them a greater chance of being their own offshoot bloodline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T10:04:18-07:00","id":102004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=101979#post101979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, it never says these guys were embraced, just that they are undead. So I've taken it as meaning they used some powerful necromantic (Entropy?) spell to become Undead but not actually die in the process and therefore keep their Avatars and Sphere magic.<br /> <br /> However, I suspect the reason they never leave Enoch is that they would Paradox explode if they came back to the material world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Liches are covered in Dead Magic, under the section on Greece and Rome. They aren't embraced - lichdom is something that a mage does to himself, pretty much. Worth a look <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T10:07:03-07:00","id":102007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=101979#post101979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except when you look at the True Black Hand/Tal'Mae'Ra stuff.<br /> <br /> As its cannon that the True Black Hand have Undead Mages (Litches) that live in Enoch and do magic. This is even talked about in the <b>Rites of Blood V20</b> book that coming out soon (or at least the drafts posted online by Eddy).<br /> <br /> Now, it never says these guys were embraced, just that they are undead. So I've taken it as meaning they used some powerful necromantic (Entropy?) spell to become Undead but not actually die in the process and therefore keep their Avatars and Sphere magic.<br /> <br /> However, I suspect the reason they never leave Enoch is that they would Paradox explode if they came back to the material world.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were probably liches. Even though liches don't really get detailed until Rev in Dead Magic. And then they are kinda oddly associated with Ancient Etruscan mages. But those guys could have gotten the rote from predecessors who went to live in dead Enoch.<br /> <br /> &lt;Shrug&gt; It's as good a way as any other at a ret-con rationalization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 03-30-2014, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T10:55:05-07:00","id":102032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=101994#post101994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The setting has some noticeable Vampires that where Ex-Mages. Some of the Antediluvians were were mystics and oracles, and may or may not have been mages, but were at least magical in some way, such as supposedly the Elder or Malkav. Cappadocius seemed to be a Mage, and Giovanni was a Necromancer (But Giovanni may have been a Sorcerer as his family magic seemed to be something passed along the family, though Dark Age Mage may have been appropriate for this). Tremere was thought to be about a thousand years old maybe when he died, along with the councile of 7 and most of the early Tremere. Baba Yaga was the most Notable Mage turned Vampire Witch. Al Ashrad was also in a similar situation as Baba Yaga and Tremere, he was a legendary Mage (Self Proclaimed greatest Wizard in the World, who even slew Haqium's favored childe).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well technically unless you got a page reference for the character sheet of when they were mortal detailing their Spheres and Arete rating whether they were Mages in game sense of the word can always be open for discussion. Could be Sorcerors for example. Or something that just never got a rulebook.<br /> <br /> Well except Tremere anyways.<br /> <br /> We're well off the beaten path here anyways. Low gen vamps seem accure hideous amounts of XP/Freebies without nessecarily having to do anything just from sheer plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2594-solomon-black","name":"Solomon Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T11:57:25-07:00","id":102084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=102007#post102007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They were probably liches. Even though liches don't really get detailed until Rev in Dead Magic. And then they are kinda oddly associated with Ancient Etruscan mages. But those guys could have gotten the rote from predecessors who went to live in dead Enoch.<br /> <br /> &lt;Shrug&gt; It's as good a way as any other at a ret-con rationalization.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to check that book out. As for the matter of the undead Mages in Enoch. Yeah like I said in my last post, I never thought they were Vampires that had kept their Avatars and Sphere Magick, I figured they were Mages that made themselves into Undead without through creative use of Sphere Magick, no vamparism involved.<br /> <br /> As for the examples Edagusto gives of &quot;former&quot; Mage's that became Vampires. Its like Solomon Black points out, Tremere (and his cronies in House Tremere) are one of the only definite former Mages (as in capital M) that became Vampires. Even then, Tremere was something like at least 300 when he turned into a Vampire anyway right? Plus it still book him and the Council of seven the better part of 50 years to translate all that Magick knowledge into a workable version of Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> The other group of former Mage's that are now Vampires is the Nagaraja bloodline. Who were a faction called the Idran and belonged to the &quot;proto&quot; -Euthanatos Tradition of Mages. They used some Kindred Vitae (no one knows from which Clan Salubri and Cappadocians are both discussed but so are the &quot;local kindred&quot; in other sources, seeing as this all happened in India that would be the Ravnos) to try and &quot;improve on&quot; the traditional Litch ritual that Mages can do (which is based on an incomplete version of the Spell of Life that makes Mummy's but is pretty much a poor imitation of the original). It screwed up and they ended up as Vampires. Suffering all the same drawbacks the Tremere did (the Nagaraja were created about 500 years before the Tremere Clan) namely they lost all their magic and gained a boat load of enemy's. Most of them died out, those that survived created a unique Path of Necromancy, a load of unique rituals and are responsible for the Thaumaturgy their sect (the Tal'Mae'Ra) have access too. <br /> <br /> So given those examples, it could be argued that former Mages turned Vampire are pretty damn good at coming up with interesting uses for Vitae and have a habit of creating new types of Blood Magic.<br /> <br /> As for individuals who may have been Mages before the embrace as opposed to confirmed groups of Mages turned into vampires:<br /> <br /> Baba Yaga and Al Ashrad and Giovanni could just as easily have been powerful Sorcerers. Admittedly Baba Yaga and Al Ashrad would have been very, very, very powerful Sorcerers to pull of the feats that are ascribed to them in fluff. However, its also easy to have a lot of this stuff be legend and myth that people have made up as the story's about these people grew over time within their respective Clans.<br /> <br /> Al Ashrad for example, pointedly acts very differently from what the story's about him say he was like pretty much every time he features in a story. Also quite famously he could not despite centuries of work and the entire Sorcerer Caste working under him break the Tremere Blood Curse on Clan Assamite.<br /> <br /> Baba Yaga did drop the Iron Curtain, which was pretty awesome and epic. However, she's a 4th Generation 5000 year old Vampire with unique blood magic, so yeah. As for having a tussle with the Nos antideluvian, it sounds like she' Verbena but the legend could have got bloated above the fact she was just a very powerful Sorceress.<br /> <br /> Giovanni I've always taken as being a Sorcerer.<br /> <br /> \u200bI do believe some of the older and now defunct fluff had Lambeth (Cappadocius's second childe) having previously been a powerful Mage. He was quite pissed off with being a vampire if I remember correctly.<br /> <br /> As for Antediluvian's that used to be Mages. One can postulate that Cappadocius and Tzimisce were. Some of the legends about them could be taken that way if you wanted. I've never seen anything really supporting the idea that any of the other Anti's were Mages before they got embraced. Malkav was a &quot;seer&quot; but I've never conceptualized that as meaning &quot;Mage&quot;.<br /> <br /> Edit - Sorted out the Nagaraja section of the post to be accurate with actual fluff rather then my half-remembered fan-theory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","user":"Hawthorn","date":". 03-31-2014, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T12:05:54-07:00","id":102091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Infernal Teddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=101855#post101855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember reading this, where was it stated?</div> </div> </div> </div>Was going to answer, but noted that posters after me covered it all in pretty full detail, so that saves me some typing... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T13:51:26-07:00","id":102139,"title":"","content":"I don't know how germane it is to talk about about which Vampire was a Mage or not. What &quot;being a mage&quot; means is such a porous term. Modern mages have a lot in common with mages during the Renaissance. A lot alike, but not quite. Both are quite different from Dark Ages Mage. If &quot;being a mage&quot; means using Sphere magic(k), I'm not sure there can be an answer to that question when there were no Spheres (which are both a game construct and a reality in the actual World of Darkness).<br /> <br /> Were these guys from the Dark Ages mages, like Tremere and his buddies? In the modern sense, probably not. Were they sorcerers, again, in the modern sense, maybe. Were they something that was both and neither? That probably hits closer to the target. Same for the bronze magic types all twisted up in the Assamite history? Probably even less likely to fit into the modern paradigm. And Baba Yaga, back in the Neolthic? Who knows?<br /> <br /> I'm guessing that the term Mage vis-a-vis modern magery probably MOST applies back in the whatever-never-never-long-ago of early Vampire history. Back in those days reality was probably pretty malleable. So many, if not most of the original 3rd could be considered mages in the modern sense. And not just Tzimisce and Cappadocius, who seem to have a sorta &quot;casting spells&quot; rep, but also Saulot (because being a seer is definitely something pretty magelike, Time Sphere?). How about Ventrue? If NWO's social engineering is &quot;magic&quot; how about one of the first guys to ever exercise his will to become a leader of humans and creator of cities? (Didn't they eventually give us all these guys actual names at some point?).<br /> <br /> BTW, In looking back at all my Order of Hermes stuff, there were DEFINITELY Primi of House Tremere who were not theparticular mage who was a founder of the Order of Hermes who was called Tremere. Is there anything anywhere that explains how he could be the long-living leader of his House and also <i>not </i>the acknowledged leader of his House?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 05-24-2017, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T15:01:19-07:00","id":102191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=102139#post102139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know how germane it is to talk about about which Vampire was a Mage or not. What &quot;being a mage&quot; means is such a porous term. Modern mages have a lot in common with mages during the Renaissance. A lot alike, but not quite. Both are quite different from Dark Ages Mage. If &quot;being a mage&quot; means using Sphere magic(k), I'm not sure there can be an answer to that question when there were no Spheres (which are both a game construct and a reality in the actual World of Darkness).<br /> <br /> Were these guys from the Dark Ages mages, like Tremere and his buddies? In the modern sense, probably not. Were they sorcerers, again, in the modern sense, maybe. Were they something that was both and neither? That probably hits closer to the target. Same for the bronze magic types all twisted up in the Assamite history? Probably even less likely to fit into the modern paradigm. And Baba Yaga, back in the Neolthics? Who knows?<br /> <br /> I'm guessing that the term Mage vis-a-vis modern magery probably MOST applies back in the whatever-never-never-long-ago of early Vampire history. Back in those days reality was probably pretty malleable. So many, if not most of the original 3rd could be considered mages in the modern sense. And not just Tzimisce and Cappadocius, who seem to have a sorta &quot;casting spells&quot; rep, but also Saulot (because being a seer is definitely something pretty magelike, Time Sphere?). How about Ventrue? If NWO's social engineering is &quot;magic&quot; how about one of the first guys to ever exercise his will to become a leader of humans and creator of cities? (Didn't they eventually give us all these guys actual names at some point).<br /> <br /> BTW, In looking back at all my Order of Hermes stuff, there were DEFINITELY Primi of House Tremere who were not Tremere. Is there anything anywhere that explains how he could be the long-living leader of his House and also not the leader of his House?</div> </div> </div> </div>Very, very good point. Probably the safest standpoint to take when ascribing &quot;magic type&quot; to people who were magical pre-Embrace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T09:44:38-07:00","id":102717,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=101979#post101979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in short Vampire Mages are not a thing, and Ghoulled Mages are screwed and grow weaker and weaker, pretty straight forward right....<br /> <br /> Except when you look at the True Black Hand/Tal'Mae'Ra stuff.<br /> <br /> As its cannon that the True Black Hand have Undead Mages (Litches) that live in Enoch and do magic. This is even talked about in the <b>Rites of Blood V20</b> book that coming out soon (or at least the drafts posted online by Eddy).<br /> <br /> Now, it never says these guys were embraced, just that they are undead. So I've taken it as meaning they used some powerful necromantic (Entropy?) spell to become Undead but not actually die in the process and therefore keep their Avatars and Sphere magic.<br /> <br /> However, I suspect the reason they never leave Enoch is that they would Paradox explode if they came back to the material world.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been awhile since I've read DSotBH, but being the DSotBH fan that I am, I'm pretty sure there are not undead Mages in the book. There are Mages in Enoch who work the Tal'Ma'Rah, but theres no Liches or anything....least not that I remember....<br /> <br /> <br /> Yea, I don't see anything like that listed here: <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Dirty_Secrets_of_the_Black_Hand\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Dirt...the_Black_Hand</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":24,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","user":"Mr Gone","date":". 03-31-2014, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T10:09:42-07:00","id":102740,"title":"","content":"There is, however, a spell for Lichdom in one of the Dead Magic books. It's not pretty, it carries some hefty consequences (I think), but it does make an undead Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T10:24:52-07:00","id":102754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=102007#post102007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They were probably liches. Even though liches don't really get detailed until Rev in Dead Magic. And then they are kinda oddly associated with Ancient Etruscan mages. But those guys could have gotten the rote from predecessors who went to live in dead Enoch.<br /> <br /> &lt;Shrug&gt; It's as good a way as any other at a ret-con rationalization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, contextual to how Liches came about in the WoD, it's actually not that strange that the first one (as indicated in DM, and DM:II) would be from an Estruscan lineage (I remember thinking how that actually made sense, when I read both books back then -- at least, again, contextual to the picture being painted...). However, I conceptually concur with you in the idea that in my world(s) liches *had* come into existence long before that, via other mystical means/corruptions of others' magic (particularly The Spell of Life, but a good couple thousand years prior to what's-his-face who got time-bubbled by the Cult of Mercury for over 2 millennia). Just saying...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=102717#post102717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's been awhile since I've read DSotBH, but being the DSotBH fan that I am, I'm pretty sure there are not undead Mages in the book. There are Mages in Enoch who work the Tal'Ma'Rah, but theres no Liches or anything....least not that I remember....<br /> <br /> <br /> Yea, I don't see anything like that listed here: <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Dirty_Secrets_of_the_Black_Hand\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Dirt...the_Black_Hand</a></div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct, sir: the mages in the Tal' were living mages (apparently/implied to be of Euthanatos and Verbena descent/extraction, particularly as that one ghoul family is derived from the latter, having Animalism, Auspex and Thaumaturgy as their disciplines). Of course, some other vampiric members could well have been mages/sorcerers in life, then embraced, but that wouldn't be that strange, contextually, and also doesn't violate any metaphysical rules of the WoD: they'd just be vampires who used to be mages, with maybe some disciplines that reflect their earlier mystical understanding, but no True Magic(k). <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T10:28:12-07:00","id":102757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=102717#post102717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's been awhile since I've read DSotBH, but being the DSotBH fan that I am, I'm pretty sure there are not undead Mages in the book. There are Mages in Enoch who work the Tal'Ma'Rah, but theres no Liches or anything....least not that I remember....<br /> <br /> Yea, I don't see anything like that listed here: <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Dirty_Secrets_of_the_Black_Hand\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Dirt...the_Black_Hand</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Funny thing, I was looking through Black Hand stuff yesterday for another thread that involved Vampires and Mages. In DSotBH your correct, it only mentions that their are Mages that live in Enoch and work for the Tal'Ma'Ra thats about it. Not much other info is given.<br /> <br /> However, looking around other sources including the Nagaraja Clan stuff that's been published since DSotBH in <b>Vampire Storytellers Handbook</b> and <b>V20 </b>and the Euthanatos stuff from their <b>Revised Tradition Book </b>along with the draft version of <b>V20 Rites of Blood</b> that were posted on the Onyx Path site a while ago, showed up some additional facts. These seem to have been retconned in from late 2nd Edition to the end of Revised and now into the V20 stuff.<br /> <br /> Basically a one of the cults of the proto-Euthanatos tradition in about 500AD performed a ritual that turned a lot of them into Liches (using their own Entopic magic and fragments of the Mummy Spell of Life). The rest of the Euthanatos took issue with this and tried to kill them all. Some of that group tried to solve this problem by doing a ritual involving Kindred Vitae, this turned those involved into the Nagaraja. Faced with the fact that the majority of their numbers had lost access to Magick and being persecuted by about 5 different groups (Euthanatos, Akashic, Kuei-Jin and Ravnos) most of them got slaughtered. The survivors (who were mainly Nagaraja but there were definitely some Litches left with them) fled into the Underworld where after a while the Tal'Ma'Ra found them and offered them safety in return for basically doing Magick for the True Black Hand. <br /> <br /> So the &quot;modern&quot; iteration of of the Tal'Ma'Ra defiantly has a cabal of Litches working for it. <br /> <br /> However, to feed back into the point of this particular thread. These guys never got embraced or even involved themselves with the second ritual involving Kindred Vitae. They used their own magics (Entropy, Life and Spirit) combined with an incomplete version of Isis's Spell of Life to make themselves into Litches.<br /> <br /> It meant the could keep true Magick while being undead but it means that they can't ever raise Arete and they have permanent paradox problems if they ever come out of the Underworld. Plus they are all pretty much insane and subject to Jhor (as in the negative &quot;amoral kill everything&quot; resonance of the Underworld), so its arguable if they are really any better off then their fellow cult members who ended up as the Nagaraja.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T10:39:51-07:00","id":102771,"title":"","content":"Gotta love retcons. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yea, I started thinking about the Nagaraja and wondered if that wasn't the connection there, since they had a vaguely Tremere-ish type origin, in which Mages were involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T18:50:41-07:00","id":103056,"title":"","content":"Personally I'm a fan of Tremere and Giovanni cultivating Mortal Sorcerers due to having Grimoires and vast resources for just that purpose.<br /> <br /> And the same with cults like the Setites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T03:38:38-07:00","id":103292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=103056#post103056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I'm a fan of Tremere and Giovanni cultivating Mortal Sorcerers due to having Grimoires and vast resources for just that purpose.<br /> <br /> And the same with cults like the Setites.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the case of the Giovanni that would make perfect sense. They were a family of necromantic sorcerers that caught the Cappadocians attention after all. Seems weird they just &quot;lost&quot; all that knowledge when a certain percentage of their family got embraced. Considering the amount of information given on the different family's that make up the Giovanni (Clan and Family) I think it would be easy to throw in some mortal/ghoul family members that have sorcery (probably just Necromantic stuff) into at least some of them. <br /> <br /> Tremere are a bit more complex. They are very much a pyramid scheme from top to bottom. Including all their mortal/ghoul resources. Sorcery potentially unbalances that paradigm. Also the fluff kinda goes back and forth on the matter of Sorcerer's and House Tremere. In some its merely stated that House Tremere had some Sorcerers in it and they were involved in the original immortality potion's that stopped working in the Dark Ages. Other fluff paints the vast majority of House Tremere (it was one of the largest Houses of the Order of Hermes) as Sorcerers including Goratrix and Tremere himself. <br /> <br /> If the former is true, I reckon the Tremere probably dropped any Sorcerer ties when the Clan became a thing. If the latter is true and they still have a metric-tone of sorcerer lore saved up in the Chantries...maybe. If they do I imagine they are keeping it quiet from the rest of the Camarilla, who are jumpy enough around Blood Magic, let alone any other sort. If I was going to the idea in a game I'd likely paint it as a choice the local Regent makes one way or the other.<br /> <br /> Setites love their mystery Cults to lure the mortals into the worship of Set. Part of that is promising secrets and power. Sorcery that actually works is a bit incentive for normal mortals. However, I think they'd drip feed any followers the knowledge. That way they keep coming back for more and they don't grow too powerful and try and mess with the Cult structure or goals or anything. Its even possible that the Setities have the largest collection of Sorcerious lore. Considering they've been collecting stuff like that since about what 5000BC? Once again I think this would be a Cult-by-Cult case though. More likely in Cults run by Setite Sorcerers. <br /> <br /> I can't really see any of the other Clan's involving themselves with Sorcery or having Ghouls/Mortal servants with access to it. <br /> <br /> The Assamites in cannon have a load of sorcery lore locked away in Alamut. However, they are very, very removed from mortal society on purpose. <br /> <br /> The Tzimisce have only ever practiced Koldunism and I'm pretty sure that a) it can't be learned by mortals and b) they would never share it with their servant even if they could. <br /> <br /> The Tal'Ma'Ra collect a load of occult lore, so many some of their revanant family's may have access to Sorcery. <br /> <br /> \u200bActually, does anyone know what happens to a Sorcerer when they get embraced? Does something about the embrace kill a persons potential for Sorcery in the same way it kills their ability to use Magick (though obviously the metaphysical mechanics will be different as Sorcerers have no Avatar).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T07:35:39-07:00","id":103377,"title":"","content":"Point of order: with the exception of mages whose Avatars have been destroyed, <i>all</i> humans have Avatars; that\u2019s where the Consensus comes from (and yes, this means that vampires aren\u2019t involved n shaping the Consensus). Mages are distinct in that their Avatars have been Awakened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T10:42:41-07:00","id":103490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=103377#post103377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point of order: with the exception of mages whose Avatars have been destroyed, <i>all</i> humans have Avatars; that\u2019s where the Consensus comes from (and yes, this means that vampires aren\u2019t involved n shaping the Consensus). Mages are distinct in that their Avatars have been Awakened.</div> </div> </div> </div>So all that has to happen is that all the mortals have to agree that all the Vampires actually are lawn chairs and always have been and then that little problem is solved, Antediluvian on down...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T10:48:55-07:00","id":103494,"title":"","content":"It's belief running a wee bit deeper than merely acknowledging the fact. There's a reason mages are often clinically insane by our standards (and all become so for a time. Quiet is no surprise)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T11:05:42-07:00","id":103499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=103292#post103292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Tremere are a bit more complex. They are very much a pyramid scheme from top to bottom. Including all their mortal/ghoul resources. Sorcery potentially unbalances that paradigm. Also the fluff kinda goes back and forth on the matter of Sorcerer's and House Tremere. In some its merely stated that House Tremere had some Sorcerers in it and they were involved in the original immortality potion's that stopped working in the Dark Ages. Other fluff paints the vast majority of House Tremere (it was one of the largest Houses of the Order of Hermes) as Sorcerers including Goratrix and Tremere himself.<br /> <br /> If the former is true, I reckon the Tremere probably dropped any Sorcerer ties when the Clan became a thing. If the latter is true and they still have a metric-tone of sorcerer lore saved up in the Chantries...maybe. If they do I imagine they are keeping it quiet from the rest of the Camarilla, who are jumpy enough around Blood Magic, let alone any other sort. If I was going to the idea in a game I'd likely paint it as a choice the local Regent makes one way or the other.<br /> <br /> Setites love their mystery Cults to lure the mortals into the worship of Set. Part of that is promising secrets and power. Sorcery that actually works is a bit incentive for normal mortals. However, I think they'd drip feed any followers the knowledge. That way they keep coming back for more and they don't grow too powerful and try and mess with the Cult structure or goals or anything. Its even possible that the Setities have the largest collection of Sorcerious lore. Considering they've been collecting stuff like that since about what 5000BC? Once again I think this would be a Cult-by-Cult case though. More likely in Cults run by Setite Sorcerers.<br /> <br /> I</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, trying to force modern conceptions of Sphere magic, Awakened vs. not Awakened magic users back on a time when things were different. The Foundation and Pillar system in Dark Ages Mage isn't really either and partakes of both. So all the members of House Tremere were Awakened mage and they weren't. Probably more &quot;were&quot; as the WHOLE of House Tremere tried to take over the Order by taking away everyone else's votes using Certamen. And Certamen just won't work without spontaneious magic. Which is Sphere magic as it is termed now. You can still see this distinction to a much lesser degree in Mage The Ascension, spontaneous magic has clearly taken over as Sphere magic and spells have become the really kinda useless Rotes. <br /> <br /> House Tremere comes from Ars Magica and those distinctions fall flat there. Every Dark Ages Order of Hermes wizard is both. There are two kinds of magic, spells and spontaneous magic. It's up to the individual wizard as to how much effort he puts into learning and mastering each of those. Some wizardslike having set effects and like the spells. Spell knowledge built faster. You can do more powerful stuff much faster if you concentrate on your spells. Spontaneous magic is harder to learn but is almost as versatile as modern Spheres and a little more versatile than Foundation and Pillar system. If anything it is more likely that House Tremere was specializing in spontaneous magic as facility in that determines potency in Certamen. Also, House Diedne were the mages who added spontaneous magic to the Order repetoire (so spontaneous magic comes from druids, I guess). It seems just as likely that House Tremere was after the deeper secrets of spontaneous magic as anything else. <br /> <br /> I think it's a good bet the derisive &quot;Tremere was a mere sorcerer&quot; is retcon propaganda by the later Order. It's not so bad if they were lost to vampirism. They were inferior in the first place. But, using that logic, Bonisagus, Trianoma, Flambeau, Guernicus, Verditus, Tytalus, etc. were all sorcerers as well. As much as they were mages. <br /> <br /> I'm guessing that the whole blood drinking fiasco definitely cut off spontaneous magic. How could it not? Now the poor Tremere were trying to hold it together without the political weapon of Certamen. They just had the pyramid going with all the voting power concentrating in the hands of a few masters (in House Tremere, your master kept your wand/vote at convocations pretty much until they were dead or you beat them in Certamen and took theirs.... that's where the pyramid of power comes from). They frantically were working to turn that storehouse of spells into a form that would work in their new form. One has to admire their genius at doing so so very quickly as an aspect of their survival. And, if you could get around the whole thing of having meetings in the day, they might have been able to pass as mortal.... They could still cast spells (of a sort). Their eeriness could just be that damn resonance thing that every wizard gets.<br /> <br /> As for the Setites, I think 5000BC might be going back a little too far. The Egyptians of 5000BC were in either the Amratian or Badarian culture which was pretty much NOTHING like what would come later. They were semi-nomadic farmer types who had some decent pottery. No stone buildings. No centralized government. No evidence of anything remotely resembling the later Pesedjet in place. 5000 years ago however, (3000 BC) you're in Predynastic/Protodynastic times where all that stuff came into being. If the Setites have something to do with Set, then they probably started about then. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T11:10:54-07:00","id":103504,"title":"","content":"I know this is kinda off-topic for this thread, but I do have a question.<br /> <br /> Every human person has an Avatar right? The vast majority are asleep but the view and beliefs of people are as a collective are still powered through these sleeping Avatars to form the Consensus of reality.<br /> <br /> Mages are different because their Avatar has woken up and can allows them to actively change reality, though not without drawback (paradox, Quiet).<br /> <br /> What about the other Supernaturals? Are they all lacking Avatars because they have ceased to be or never where human? Does this exempt them from deciding how reality works?<br /> <br /> If so and considering the program and consensus manipulation that the Technoracy have been up to for the last 400 years or so why have Vampire, Werewolves and Demons not popped out of existence the way that a lot of the Bygone creatures that now just live in the Umbra did?<br /> <br /> Edit - Ajax, I once again see your point. Its still a new idea for me to try and wrap my head around the concept the very nature of magic has changed a few times over the course of human civilization. <br /> <br /> As for the Setite thing...don't get me started.<br /> <br /> I'm no historian but even basic study of civilizations pre-sorta 3000BC from wikipedia paint a very, very different story then the Vampire background/history in Masquerade. The Egyptian Gods were around since at least 8000BC in the Vampire Timeline (and to be fair were actual Gods) and Set and his Clan (the Setites) had been hording occult knowledge since the &quot;Second City&quot; which was supposedly founded about 7300BC. <br /> <br /> Some of the cannon Vampires are even older then that I think Baba Yaga is 7,000 and Ur-Shulgi's 9.000. Even worse the Vampire that kills Babay Yaga is supposed to be &quot;double&quot; her age making her 14,000 years old (as in 12,000BC). <br /> <br /> Basically, in the past I've run with the idea that Vampire really, really have their dates wrong (entirely possible, anything pre-Egypt is treated as myth by most modern Vampires) or the worlds history is just a lot more occluded and different in the CWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","user":"Hawthorn","date":". 04-01-2014, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T12:11:10-07:00","id":103547,"title":"","content":"For the most part, no the other supernaturals do not have Avatars, and they do not cause Paradox if they see things (so they probably have little sway on the consensus). They do seem to have some sort of strong cosmological backing, though, Vampires and Demons come from God, Werewolves and Ghosts are linked to various parts of the Umbra, etc. That's the most likely reason they are more resistant(although you'll give yourself a headache trying to figure out why those aspects of reality are not beholden to the consensus).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T16:39:02-07:00","id":103708,"title":"","content":"I like to draw a distinction between \u201cthe Consensus\u201d (which is how humans believe the world works) and \u201creality\u201d (which is how the world <i>actually</i> works). Needless to say, the Consensus can <i>influence</i> reality; but it is not all-powerful. These are, after all, Sleeper Avatars we\u2019re dealing with here: while they are able to achieve in aggregate what individual Sleeping Avatars cannot achieve, some things are harder to change than others \u2014 and some things are <i>so</i> hard to change that even the cumulative belief of every Sleeper currently on the planet may not be enough to change them. Turning every vampire into a lawn chair \u201csimply\u201d by making everyone on the planet believe that vampires are actually lawnchairs is probably one of those things; likewise with \u201cdisbelieving\u201d them out of existence. <br /> <br /> And bear in mind that it\u2019s largely a moot point, as the Consensus isn\u2019t anywhere <i>close</i> to saying that vampires don\u2019t exist: there\u2019s a heck of a lot more to the world than Western society. So whether or not a unified Consensus could eradicate vampires is an unanswerable question, because the Consensus isn\u2019t unified. Which is not to say that the Technocracy isn\u2019t trying. <br /> <br /> To take another example, the Consensus has no say as to the nature of the Umbra; at best, it can influence the nature of the Gauntlet and make the Umbra easier or harder to reach. But the Umbra itself is outside of the Consensus\u2019 sphere of influence. If you could get large settlements of humans with Avatars living in the Umbra without turning into spirits and <i>losing</i> their Avatars, you <i>might</i> eventually change this; but that\u2019s a lot of conditions that we\u2019re nowhere <i>close</i> to achieving. Spirits (and by extension werewolves) probably have additional protection against the Consensus due to their connection to the Umbra. Wraiths are safely hidden away in an Umbral layer and are beyond the Consensus\u2019 reach. <br /> <br /> Changelings are an interesting case, in that they arguably <i>are</i> being edited out of existence by a hostile Consensus of humanity; that is, after all, a major theme of <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b>: people by and large don\u2019t believe in fairies anymore, and the fae are suffering for it. Put another way, Banality is arguably a manifestation of the Consensus \u2014 at least in part. The fae are probably unusually vulnerable to the Consensus due to the strong connection between the Dreaming and human dreams, which are themselves closely related to belief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T04:54:11-07:00","id":103965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=103708#post103708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings are an interesting case, in that they arguably <i>are</i> being edited out of existence by a hostile Consensus of humanity; that is, after all, a major theme of <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b>: people by and large don\u2019t believe in fairies anymore, and the fae are suffering for it. Put another way, Banality is arguably a manifestation of the Consensus \u2014 at least in part. The fae are probably unusually vulnerable to the Consensus due to the strong connection between the Dreaming and human dreams, which are themselves closely related to belief.</div> </div> </div> </div>Banality may be a manifestation of the consensus (sort of), but it is not a rejection of the fae directly; arguably that happened a long time ago. Instead it is more the nature of the current consensus is creating a hostile environment, much as would happen to Vampires or Werewolves if somehow the masses believed in an endless day or a world of silver grass. It's not quite the same thing as the consensus isn't actually removing people's ability to dream, but its a good approximation.<br /> <br /> To put it another way, the Fae arguably do have a higher metaphysical backing, it just happens that backing is vulnerable to something on earth. As it is pushed away, so are they.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T07:34:57-07:00","id":104037,"title":"","content":"Seems that the general idea that the Consensus and Reality are two separate things does provide a good explanation for why the other major Supernaturals of the World of Darkness are still around for the most part.<br /> <br /> Even if you don't make that division we can explain the continued existence of the majority of Supernatural creatures thus:<br /> <br /> As Dataweaver mentions the Consensus has no impact on the Umbra (save for the bits it does I guess like the Dreaming) allows for at least a plausible explanation for Wraiths, Mummy's, Kuei-Jin, Werewolves and other Changing Breeds. Since they all have a link to or a &quot;umbral&quot; nature inherently.<br /> <br /> Changelings/Fae might have had the same type of immunity once upon a time, but as Ramnesis said, their metaphysical backing was vulnerable to something the Consensus can effect and therefore they are getting screwed over by it now. <br /> <br /> This still leaves Vampires and Demons as the odd ones out.<br /> <br /> Demons are sorta extra-planar (to borrow a D&amp;D term) in that one could argue that have a link to a realm beyond the physical. Likewise they are very rooted within a human hosts soul (if we are talking about the Fallen) so the have an &quot;anchor&quot; to resist reality rejecting them. <br /> <br /> With Vampires you can as Ramnesis says say &quot;God did it!&quot; and that be the end of it if you want. Nothing else massively springs to mind about why Vampire don't suffer from it.<br /> <br /> However, one could argue that enough people still believe in Demons (it's a surprisingly common belief even among secular people) for them to have no problem with Consensus. Vampire saturate modern culture and have for about the last 100 years on and off more or less. So while people might not believe in them, their perfectly happy to think about and engage with the idea of vampires. Hence the Consensus leaves Vampire alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T09:05:54-07:00","id":104080,"title":"","content":"Demons vis-a-vis Demon created Reality. They can use exploits on Reality. They can hack the basecode of Reality if they were in on development and implementation. The only way they care about your belief is because it's juice, it makes them feel good and that's what the point of the whole Rebellion was about in the first place for many of them. <br /> <br /> God created Vampires. Alternatively, Angels (not Fallen) created Vampires. In either case, see above. <br /> <br /> Also, Kuei-jin and the Imbued also got &quot;written in&quot; as well. <br /> <br /> But, all in all, the game lines don't cross well at these levels or at least, take a lot of jury-rigging and cherry-picking about who is right, Werewolves or Mages? How does Vampire and Demon sync with that, or can it? Can we brdige those using Kindred of the East and throw in the Imbued?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T10:33:37-07:00","id":104138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=104080#post104080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But, all in all, the game lines don't cross well at these levels or at least, take a lot of jury-rigging and cherry-picking about who is right, Werewolves or Mages? How does Vampire and Demon sync with that, or can it? Can we brdige those using Kindred of the East and throw in the Imbued?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I generally agree with this point.<br /> <br /> NWoD lets you cross them and have them basically &quot;shrug&quot; at the fact that their metaphysics just don't cross over for the most part (or at least not in ways your average splat is aware of). They can point out odd parallels and coincidences and suck and dig into that if they want. Up the ST if there is anything too that or not. <br /> <br /> CWoD requires that an ST be selective about his use of fluff for all game lines involved. Likewise, if he decided to stick to the cannon meta stuff for say both Vampire and Mage, he's going to have to emphasize the few places they might cross to make it work. Straight out of the box one could argue that they simple don't work. I think the V20, W20, M20 and Wa20 new generation of CWoD books is making it easier by going with a more &quot;decide&quot; your own cannon approach to things. <br /> <br /> Personally, I'd never cross more then two game lines. Prior to digging into Mage in the last month I've been a pure Masquerade player pretty much for the last 10 years. Read up on Demon and Mummy a bit. Werewolf and Wraith even less and I think I've ever even picked up a Changeling the Dreaming book.<br /> <br /> In that whole time I've only ever crossed it over as an ST with Kindred of the East and bits of Werewolf (namely that they exist and hate Vampires/keep them in the cities), oh and used generic ghosts removed from any of the Wraith stuff. Never felt the game suffered for lacking content. Each of the CWoD lines is chock full of fluff, lore and unique stuff that gives your more the enough toys to fill a world. <br /> <br /> As a player I've been in Masquerade games that crossed over with but no more then the extent I've crossed it over in my games, Mage (there was a local Verbena, got killed by some Technocracy), Changeling (we had a Kaysid in the group), Wraith (there was a civil war in one of the underworld cities that a few dead characters got involved in off screen) and Kindred of the East. Some of these worked really well some not so much. <br /> <br /> My general rule is don't let the splats cross the streams (no Mage Vampires) and try and keep everything deeply personal for the PC's. With what I've learned about Mage I might cross over those two once I've got a copy of M20. However, I'd emphasize the points where the fluff cross-over e.g. the Tremere and Ta'Ma'Ra and I'd very much have my players either as all Vampires or all Mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T12:25:09-07:00","id":104244,"title":"","content":"In Sorcerer Revised, it talks about how consensus / paradox may or may not affect the various supernaturals. When it mentions Vampires, it suggests the explanation that the blood cost each night is them paying off the paradox of their static / undead existence. Likewise for blood powering their disciplines. It does not mention how that interacts with powers that don't use blood, but really, the vampiric state involves siphoning portions of the spirit, prime, and life out of other entities, and concentrating it into tass. So, just having a few points of tass contained within you seems to provide certain benefits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>&quot;Maturity is knowing you were an idiot in the past.&quot;<br /> &quot;If that's true, then Wisdom is knowing you'll be an idiot in the future.&quot;<br /> &quot;And Common Sense is knowing that you should try not to be an idiot NOW.&quot;<br /> -Questionable Content 976</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1042-zhyzhaksmate","name":"ZhyzhaksMate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1042_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T12:26:09-07:00","id":104246,"title":"","content":"Having come across as someone who doesn't &quot;cross the streams&quot;, I have to admit I do so relentlessly. Almost religiously.<br /> <br /> I ran a Mage game that ran for... four years? three? where I did a lot of crossing over. We took breaks from the main action to play 4-8 weeks &quot;sub&quot; chronicles - one was Wraith and and one was Vampire. We were planning on a third Changeling one, but we wrapped up the game before that. (It went off the rails into weird archetypes and philosophy and time travel...). All three were directly integrated into several plot points and they also shared elements (a magic Device, some NPCs, etc.) in common as well. They definitely interacted with one pack of werewolves (and then, later, with their predecessors from a century plus before). I ran all of the above by their own intrinsic rules (with attendant throwing out the window when necessary for a good story). <br /> <br /> It was also a city-based Mage game. Which is a lot harder than it sounds. I think they left the city and the suburbs exactly once in all that time. To go to Hawaii when they were in the future. The rest of the time they stayed within ~50 miles of St. Louis and usually were within the greater metro area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T10:17:39-07:00","id":110151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=101979#post101979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Far as I understand it (and I am a complete novice at Ascension stuff) when a Mage gets Embraced he stops being a Mage.<br /> <br /> H<br /> Except when you look at the True Black Hand/Tal'Mae'Ra stuff.<br /> <br /> As its cannon that the True Black Hand have Undead Mages (Litches) that live in Enoch and do magic. This is even talked about in the <b>Rites of Blood V20</b> book that coming out soon (or at least the drafts posted online by Eddy).<br /> <br /> Now, it never says these guys were embraced, just that they are undead. So I've taken it as meaning they used some powerful necromantic (Entropy?) spell to become Undead but not actually die in the process and therefore keep their Avatars and Sphere magic.<br /> <br /> However, I suspect the reason they never leave Enoch is that they would Paradox explode if they came back to the material world.</div> </div> </div> </div>maybe someone already answered this but these liches are a form of undead which explicitly maintain mage powers(just can't increase arete) there was a rote in dead magic 1. and yeah it pretty much says that paradox would strike them pretty hard particularly since theyve lived so long","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T10:36:50-07:00","id":110158,"title":"","content":"also i think i read somewhere that part of the reason paradox doesn't strike down werewolves and msot other splats is because their powers are largely static. its also mentioned that the things they do sometimes lie(barely) withing the limits of the consesnus. and thus exploiting that. a mage creating a fireball is(whether he believes it or not) rewriting reality . at least thats how i understand it. a blood mage or sorcerer produces the same effect in a different way. maybe even taking advantage of some ( however limited) &quot;residual&quot; background belief in the supernatural.<br /> though this is just a theory<br /> or as one book put it<br /> &quot;a mage teaches the dog(earth-consensus) a new trick evey single time and it might bite him back<br /> &quot;a sorcerer tells it to do sth it once did before and still does just less frequently.<br /> this is perhaps an oversimplification but i think it's a relative good explanation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T07:50:04-07:00","id":110789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=104037#post104037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Dataweaver mentions the Consensus has no impact on the Umbra (save for the bits it does I guess like the Dreaming) allows for at least a plausible explanation for Wraiths, Mummy's, Kuei-Jin, Werewolves and other Changing Breeds. Since they all have a link to or a &quot;umbral&quot; nature inherently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nitpick: the Dreaming isn\u2019t part of the Umbra\u2026 probably. It\u2019s possible (but not certain) that the Zone known as the Maya is the Dreaming; it\u2019s also possible that it\u2019s either a part of the Dreaming or something related to the Dreaming. Either way, it\u2019s a Zone \u2014 which means that it\u2019s <i>connected</i> to the Umbra, but is not technically <i>part of</i> the Umbra. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T09:09:27-07:00","id":110829,"title":"","content":"Nothing special. As most people have already said, when a vampire Embraces a mage you just wind up with a vampire. The Avatar goes bye-bye. That's it. You start from square one. I believe there were some (entirely optional) rules for an ST to allow players to liquidate the XP from their Spheres and use it to buy Disciplines, or possibly even Thaumaturgy Paths and Rituals. Certainly Sorcerers had that option back in second edition (ditto for Sorcerers who Awakened or somehow became wraiths). But for the most part, you just wind up with a neonate vamp.<br /> <br /> Of course, said vampire will retain all of the knowledge he had as a mage, meaning he knows all about the various factions, their metaphysics, who's who, where the chantries are, etc. He might not be able to work Sphere magick anymore, but that he still has the potential to be dangerous. He might even be able to eventually translate some of his former knowledge into new Rituals, a new Path or even an entirely new school of blood magic (see the aforementioned part about converting XP above). Personally I think that works better for sorcerers, psychics and other static, linear magics. Indeed, IIRC some of the later material for Dark Ages hinted that Tremere might have been a sorcerer rather than a true mage. Then again, the Tzimisce also claim that the Eldest was a true, Awakened mage (or at least they did back in second edition). Various other characters like al-Ashrad have been called magicians or sorcerers before their Embrace, but its never been explicitly stated if they were true mages, sorcerers or something else altogether.<br /> <br /> As for Liches, yeah, that's a Rote from <b>Dead Magic</b>. It's mostly a Etruscan and Greek thing so by the modern era Euthanatoi and maybe Hermetics are the most acquainted with it (and aren't inclined to share or practice their knowledge anyway), though the Chakravanti had developed their own version called <i>Yamasattva</i>. They aren't vampires or wraiths, they are mages who have discovered a special, magical state of undeath, though the results are not pleasant to say the least. They do lose their Avatar, and the ability to learn new magic, but otherwise they retain their old abilities. Presumably these are the same Liches mentioned in <b>Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand</b>, though we can't know for certain (DSOTBH was written for second edition, and included abominations, soul eaters, and other stuff that didn't really get used much afterwards; its entirely possible their liches were intended to be Embraced mages who retained true magick...).<br /> <br /> Intriguingly, various sources for both Vampire and Mage claimed the Nagaraja bloodline were the Idran, a fallen Chakravanti sect of necromancers who used a variant of the <i>Yamasattva</i> rote to transform themselves into a new lineage of vampires rather than liches. Of course, the Chakravanti (or at least the Idran) had contact with the Black Hand, and the Nagaraja bloodline was affiliated with that sect, so its also possible that the liches of the Tal'mahe'ra were just vanilla liches after all.<br /> <br /> However, that brings up another interesting point. Several sources have hinted at mages using magic to teach vampires. <b>Veil of Night</b> mentioned the Ahl-i-Batin teaching the Ashirra the rudiments of Sihr. DSOTBH had the Chakravanti (or at least the fallen Idran sect) and Verbena teaching the Tal'mahe'ra, even spawning the Rafastio family and the Nagaraja bloodline. Some second edition material had Native American Dreamspeakers associating with the Sabbat in the American Southwest, while Dark Ages material suggested House Tytalus helped the Tzimisce refine Koldunic Sorcery. While most of its just fluff, at least it gives some hint that the metaphysics of true magick <i>might</i> overlap with the principles of Thaumaturgy and other forms of blood magic, however slightly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1449-zakariya-ali-sher","name":"Zakariya Ali Sher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T16:13:38-07:00","id":111094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=110151#post110151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> maybe someone already answered this but these liches are a form of undead which explicitly maintain mage powers(just can't increase arete) there was a rote in dead magic 1. and yeah it pretty much says that paradox would strike them pretty hard particularly since theyve lived so long</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you know which chapter of the book they are covered in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2256-goblin404","name":"Goblin404","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2256_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T16:43:34-07:00","id":111120,"title":"","content":"Not sure of the page number off hand, but its in the chapter on Greco-Roman magic. Its' quite an extensive Rote too; there are several pages worth of discussion and mechanics for it. TB: Euthanatos revised has a little bit on Lichdom too, and some related Rotes (Necrosynthesis), but they don't reprint the original Lichdom Rote.<br /> <br /> Also: Dead Magic II has a couple of necromancy Rotes in the Etruscan chapter, and information on Nesna Nethshrac, a Lich NPC, but it too did not reprint the original Lichdom Rote (though it does discuss Etruscan history, divination and their views on the underworld).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1449,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1449-zakariya-ali-sher","user":"Zakariya Ali Sher","date":". 04-11-2014, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1449-zakariya-ali-sher","name":"Zakariya Ali Sher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T18:28:55-07:00","id":111154,"title":"","content":"Pertaining to the Liches of the Tal'Mahe'Ra, &quot;Lich&quot; is used as a title rather than the literal form. To quote V20's Companion:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lich (Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra; 4-point Title)<br /> The Liches of the True Black Hand are what remains<br /> of puissant and evil mortal mages who have sworn<br /> themselves to the Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra\u2019s cause and employed<br /> soul-excoriating rituals in order to preserve themselves<br /> in the state of hellish immortality conferred by<br /> vampirism. Although the Embrace extinguishes the<br /> spark of cosmic enlightenment that allows true mages<br /> to impose their wills on the world, it doesn\u2019t destroy<br /> the knowledge that these wicked creatures accumulated<br /> before joining the ranks of the Damned </div> </div> </div>From Dirty Secret of the Black Hand, it was the same:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Del'Roh is served by three powerful Kindred, called the liches, who used to be Euthanatos mages. they serve as judges and representatives of the Del'Roh. They are cruel, powerful and zealous, making them the greatest threat to the secret factions within the Black Hand. </div> </div> </div>In V20's Children of the Revolution, there's also a character named Roderigo Al-Dakhil, Lich of the Dead City. He's a Kindred all the way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/78-bloodarmor","name":"BloodArmor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar78_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T19:56:25-07:00","id":111193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BloodArmor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=111154#post111154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pertaining to the Liches of the Tal'Mahe'Ra, &quot;Lich&quot; is used as a title rather than the literal form. Dirty Secret of the Black Hand, it was the same</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's going to bug the hell out of me now. Since reading the Idran stuff that said that some of that faction that survived and fled into the Underworld were Litches (as in Mages who enacted that rote on themselves). Likewise, its not just that old fluff the rough draft version of <b>V20 Rites of Blood</b> that Eddie posted up mentions that the Tal'Mae'Ra has &quot;undead&quot; (meaning Litch) Mages among its ranks.<br /> <br /> Not to first time two WoD sources have contradicted each other. Still I was hoping the V20 line would kinda straighten issues like this out a bit. I guess its ultimately up the ST in that case. Though isn't it always! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T23:45:23-07:00","id":111313,"title":"","content":"So one could consider the blood point spent as a blood sacrifice. There are a lot of interesting ties to the shadow lands with vampires. They remember things that nothing else walking the earth does. I wonder how many ghosts and ghosts of buildings linger just because antediluvians continue to exist and remember them. I wonder what vanishes in the hereafter when an antediluvian is diablorized","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>there are no bad ideas, just ideas that have not been refined enough","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1608-iamthesweeper","name":"IAmTheSweeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T08:04:05-07:00","id":114064,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BloodArmor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=111154#post111154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pertaining to the Liches of the Tal'Mahe'Ra, &quot;Lich&quot; is used as a title rather than the literal form. To quote V20's Companion:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lich (Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra; 4-point Title)<br /> The Liches of the True Black Hand are what remains<br /> of puissant and evil mortal mages who have sworn<br /> themselves to the Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra\u2019s cause and employed<br /> soul-excoriating rituals in order to preserve themselves<br /> in the state of hellish immortality conferred by<br /> vampirism. Although the Embrace extinguishes the<br /> spark of cosmic enlightenment that allows true mages<br /> to impose their wills on the world, it doesn\u2019t destroy<br /> the knowledge that these wicked creatures accumulated </div> </div> </div><br /> From Dirty Secret of the Black Hand, it was the same:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Del'Roh is served by three powerful Kindred, called the liches, who used to be Euthanatos mages. they serve as judges and representatives of the Del'Roh. They are cruel, powerful and zealous, making them the greatest threat to the secret factions within the Black Hand. </div> </div> </div><br /> In V20's Children of the Revolution, there's also a character named Roderigo Al-Dakhil, Lich of the Dead City. He's a Kindred all the way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I didn't even think about the Tal'Mahe'Ra stuff from V20.... Thanks for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T20:55:20-07:00","id":114520,"title":"","content":"As of Mage Revised the True Black Hand &quot;Liches&quot; were proto-Euthanatos who subjected themselves to an independently developed variation of the rite in Dead Magic. Some members of the sect went on to found the Nagaraja bloodline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T06:46:26-07:00","id":115255,"title":"","content":"I have been playing Mage/Ascention and Vampire/masquerade for many years. Pretty much since they came out. In the Tremere revised clanbook, It kind of elaborates on the fact that, Tremere will watch those who show magical promise, sometimes for quite a while. They will only Ghoul/blood bond those who appear after many years to not be able to awaken. Because they still have magical potential they are sort of the creme de la creme of potential Thaumaturges. Even then they only blood bond the promising, the less promising are ghouled and put into service of the clan in lesser more demeaning roles. A Tremere will attempt to befriend and potentially blood bond (and by blood bond, I mean the, you get three drops and feel a supernatural affinity for the vampire, not ghouling) an awakened mage, and usually only if that mage has &quot;hermetic&quot; house Tremere like abilities. They might befriend a cultest or an etherite just because hell why not, it's cool having an awakened ally. Plus, depending on the mage themselves, they might view the Tremere as a sort of hedge mage ally. In the original &quot;Book of Shadows, Mage players guide&quot;, There are merits for having a vampire/werewolf/changling companions. I believe they are all 4 point supernatural merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2764-rory-asmodeus-carroll","name":"Rory \"Asmodeus\" Carroll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T19:13:44-07:00","id":1095713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=101930#post101930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, for a similar reason: when you die, your Avatar goes away. So there are no wraiths with Avatars, meaning that no Risen have Avatars either. <b>The same holds true for mummies</b>. And before you ask: you won\u2019t find any werewolves, changelings, or demons with Avatars either. You will only find Avatars in ordinary,,live human beings</div> </div> </div> </div>(That's what I get for not checking my messages properly -- somebody linked me a message about this comment and I didn't note it until just tonight... been busy with business and travel...)<br /> <br /> Bold: Much like with Liches, this is less true. Mummies *do* have their Avatars -- they call them Sahu(s). They are the aspect of the old Egyptian mages that made them mages. Their Sahus/god-selves, however, are restructured by the Spell of Life into a different metaphysical purpose. This is similar -- though of course also markedly different in several ways -- to how a lich's Avatar is (at least partially) reworked to be bound to their undead selves. (Sidenote: as conjectured by a number of mages, werewolves and certain other living supernatural beings may also have &quot;avatars&quot;, but their god-souls are reworked/repurposed in a different manner, and are not Avatars(tm) in the sense that mages understand. Much like with garou, etc., the (A)vatars of mummies are integrated and &quot;cemented&quot; into their metaphysical identities more tightly than even with mages and their Avatars, so they don't have the open-ended connection to the raw power of the universe the same way mages do... though mummies' particular paradigm -- backed by the metaphysical link of their &quot;united&quot; god-selves along with Horus and Ra -- *does* go a long way to compensating for this by making the magic they do possess very potent within its delineations.)<br /> <br /> This is rarely, however, an important metaphysical point for the vast majority of circumstances. Only in very specific, very select moments would the metaphysical point actually have any important bearing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T19:25:52-07:00","id":1095716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=101930#post101930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, for a similar reason: when you die, your Avatar goes away. So there are no wraiths with Avatars, meaning that no Risen have Avatars either. The same holds true for mummies. And before you ask: you won\u2019t find any werewolves, changelings, or demons with Avatars either. You will only find Avatars in ordinary,,live human beings</div> </div> </div> </div>And occasionally Technocratic Constructs. The robots/clones. Not the buildings.<br /> <br /> Also as others mentioned. Lich's. But those are a specific exception to a general rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T21:56:18-07:00","id":1095758,"title":"","content":"Wraiths have a background called Eidelon a mysterious &quot;Higher&quot; self above the Psyche that pushes the Wraith towards transcendence. It functions and acts in all ways like an Avatar its just not giving you kewl powerz..... so saying Wraiths lack an avatar is what I'd say is a misunderstanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T15:45:58-07:00","id":1096065,"title":"","content":"Mummy Sahus and Wraith Eidolons do each bear some resemblance to the Avatar in their own way; but I'm unconvinced that they're the same thing. Ultimately though, it's a moot point: there are no Awakened mummies or wraiths, as they lose whatever it is that lets one access the Spheres when they become mummies or wraiths, if not sooner. With the sole and arguable exception that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11744\" data-vbnamecard=\"11744\">Enginseer-42</a> pointed out, I stand by my original assertion: you need to be human to be a Mage. (I say \u201carguable exception\u201d because a case could be made that those constructs who have Avatars <i>are</i> humans, despite their artificial origins.)<br /> <br /> And while I'm here, I'd like to point out that V20 Black Hand effectively put to rest the notion of vampires with Avatars: they have vampires who can wield Awakened magic, but only with the cooperation of a mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T18:32:51-07:00","id":1096126,"title":"","content":"Well. I meant ACTUAL Liches. Not Vampires who call themselves Liches. Liches are corpses who've had the living mages avatar soaked into the body. Difficult thing to do, but the results are certainly notable in that they're one of the hardest things to kill I've ever seen if built right. The 'rote' to become a Lich is in Dead Magic. And essentially requires mastery of all spheres. Or almost all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T23:34:46-07:00","id":1096182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=1096065#post1096065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mummy Sahus and Wraith Eidolons do each bear some resemblance to the Avatar in their own way; but I'm unconvinced that they're the same thing. Ultimately though, it's a moot point: there are no Awakened mummies or wraiths, as they lose whatever it is that lets one access the Spheres when they become mummies or wraiths, if not sooner. With the sole and arguable exception that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11744\" data-vbnamecard=\"11744\">Enginseer-42</a> pointed out, I stand by my original assertion: you need to be human to be a Mage. (I say \u201carguable exception\u201d because a case could be made that those constructs who have Avatars <i>are</i> humans, despite their artificial origins.)<br /> <br /> And while I'm here, I'd like to point out that V20 Black Hand effectively put to rest the notion of vampires with Avatars: they have vampires who can wield Awakened magic, but only with the cooperation of a mage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I don't think anyone should be getting new out of game mechanics for potentially having an avatar(no wraith/mummy/vampire mages) but rather their avatar is in a different state than A mages thus giving different properties but continuing its general drive to push the character towards Ascension/trancendence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T11:24:54-07:00","id":1096421,"title":"","content":"The only time I saw somebody manage to semi-RAW rules-lawyer-wiggle themselves into an actual book-supported argument for having True Magick as a non-pure-human was through very unfortunate writing in the Sorceror 2nd Edition book...<br /> <br /> It goes like this:<br /> <br /> 1) Sorceror 2nd Ed states that sorcery works through the sleeping avatar.<br /> 2) Bastet. Kitsune etc. have a merit that allows them to use sorcery. Which is fine because homids technically have a sleeping avatar that can never awaken...<br /> 3) Sorceror 2nd Ed has a merit that allows sorcerors to use bursts of uncontrolled Wild True Magick from their still asleep avatar<br /> 4) Me: HNNNNNNNGH:...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T13:11:34-07:00","id":1096457,"title":"","content":"<b>V20 Black Hand</b> specifically allows its Archaic Sorcerers (read: DAMage rules) to \u201cloan\u201d their Avatars to vampires, allowing those vampires to use their Archaic Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T01:38:13-07:00","id":1097457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=1095713#post1095713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(That's what I get for not checking my messages properly -- somebody linked me a message about this comment and I didn't note it until just tonight... been busy with business and travel...)<br /> <br /> Bold: Much like with Liches, this is less true. Mummies *do* have their Avatars -- they call them Sahu(s). They are the aspect of the old Egyptian mages that made them mages. Their Sahus/god-selves, however, are restructured by the Spell of Life into a different metaphysical purpose. This is similar -- though of course also markedly different in several ways -- to how a lich's Avatar is (at least partially) reworked to be bound to their undead selves. (Sidenote: as conjectured by a number of mages, werewolves and certain other living supernatural beings may also have &quot;avatars&quot;, but their god-souls are reworked/repurposed in a different manner, and are not Avatars(tm) in the sense that mages understand. Much like with garou, etc., the (A)vatars of mummies are integrated and &quot;cemented&quot; into their metaphysical identities more tightly than even with mages and their Avatars, so they don't have the open-ended connection to the raw power of the universe the same way mages do... though mummies' particular paradigm -- backed by the metaphysical link of their &quot;united&quot; god-selves along with Horus and Ra -- *does* go a long way to compensating for this by making the magic they do possess very potent within its delineations.)<br /> <br /> This is rarely, however, an important metaphysical point for the vast majority of circumstances. Only in very specific, very select moments would the metaphysical point actually have any important bearing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> t think is a simpler way of explaining this is to say that mages avatars are like &quot;raw&quot; diamonds- infinite potential but.. not really good at anything..and indeed are not &quot;something&quot;<br /> whereas the werewolves is one with a particular shape and purpse","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T13:21:56-07:00","id":1102898,"title":"","content":"From the looks of this question, because of it's frequency, it might be in that book of secrets FAQ that Satyros mentioned the BoS having..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i57.tinypic.com/10r2rtu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1779-spider_one","name":"spider_one","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T13:30:30-07:00","id":1102902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>spider_one</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=1102898#post1102898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the looks of this question, because of it's frequency, it might be in that book of secrets FAQ that Satyros mentioned the BoS having..</div> </div> </div> </div>Well hopefully we can get our hands on it in the coming weeks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T08:42:03-07:00","id":1103820,"title":"","content":"Marconius, the first Kiasyd, was a Magus, as was his sister. Marconius's sire (a fourth Generation Lasombra) had no clue about his magic arts, he simply embraced a nobleman who owned land he wanted under his power. Marc proceeded to decide he was too cool to be a Lasombra, and using his knowledge from his life as a Mage he did... Something. Lore of the Bloodlines explains it nicely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T15:04:23-07:00","id":1104495,"title":"","content":"From the FAQ:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <b>If My Mage Gets Embraced, Can She Still Use Sphere Magick?</b><br /> Unless your Storyteller decides to Golden Rule a system that\u2019s been in place since The Book of Shadows in 1994, no. Seriously, NO. Please stop asking this question. Fer Realsies. <br /> <br /> That said, I appreciate your other questions. (Just not that one.) Your questions show you care, and we all thank you for that!</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T17:24:28-07:00","id":1104549,"title":"","content":"XDXDXD<br /> <br /> True...But, if your mage get's embraced by a 7th generation or lower, and then joins the Tal'mahe'Ra, and learn the Aupex 6 + I don't remember what Combined Discipline that allows to take an Avatar with all and the knowledge of Spheres from your mage victim...then you can use Sphere Magick for the rather long duration of that power.<br /> <br /> Now you only need to coinvince your ST to allow you to start your unlife as an Abomination...with Kiasyd blood...and you're done. :P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T06:07:00-07:00","id":1105352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=1104549#post1104549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">XDXDXD<br /> <br /> True...But, if your mage get's embraced by a 7th generation or lower, and then joins the Tal'mahe'Ra, and learn the Aupex 6 + I don't remember what Combined Discipline that allows to take an Avatar with all and the knowledge of Spheres from your mage victim...then you can use Sphere Magick for the rather long duration of that power.<br /> <br /> Now you only need to coinvince your ST to allow you to start your unlife as an Abomination...with Kiasyd blood...and you're done. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the last character I saw like that ended up as a soulforged ashtray on a Hierarch's desk.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T09:38:45-07:00","id":1105426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=1104549#post1104549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">XDXDXD<br /> <br /> True...But, if your mage get's embraced by a 7th generation or lower, and then joins the Tal'mahe'Ra, and learn the Aupex 6 + I don't remember what Combined Discipline that allows to take an Avatar with all and the knowledge of Spheres from your mage victim...then you can use Sphere Magick for the rather long duration of that power.<br /> <br /> Now you only need to coinvince your ST to allow you to start your unlife as an Abomination...with Kiasyd blood...and you're done. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Where can I find this magick stealing Combo?<br /> It would be the perfect power for the 5 dot enemy flaw that is pictured as the beautiful prince(ss) of Cologne in the backstory.<br /> <br /> Some flaws are totally not worth their points.<br /> If a ST is only a little sadistic you shouldn't give him a nice little old vampire to play with...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T11:07:51-07:00","id":1105456,"title":"","content":"1) Shove your avatar into an object (creating a phylactery)<br /> 2) Get embraced<br /> 3) ...<br /> 4) Profit<br /> <br /> Edit: Im only joking, but i've seen worse things around my groups table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T11:20:56-07:00","id":1105465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=1105426#post1105426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where can I find this magick stealing Combo?<br /> It would be the perfect power for the 5 dot enemy flaw that is pictured as the beautiful prince(ss) of Cologne in the backstory.<br /> <br /> Some flaws are totally not worth their points.<br /> If a ST is only a little sadistic you shouldn't give him a nice little old vampire to play with...</div> </div> </div> </div>The V20 Black hand book, page 153. It can be done either via the mage (using a bastardized version of chakravanti Foundation and Pillars) or via a Dominate 6/Auspex 5 combo Discipline","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T13:02:36-07:00","id":1105493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Shove your avatar into an object (creating a phylactery)<br /> 2) Get embraced<br /> 3) ...<br /> 4) Profit<br /> <br /> Edit: Im only joking, but i've seen worse things around my groups table.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've heard of that reasoning before...and it has it's merit.<br /> <br /> One of the problems of undead in mage is the idea that the avatar leaves the body in the moment of death...but if your avatar it's trapped in an object, then it doesn't go away.<br /> <br /> This it's one of the ways the canon Lich rite (of Dead Magic) can be performed without needing Spirit. <br /> <br /> Of course, being vampire it's different from being a Lich, so the ST can easily say that the same principle doesn't apply because the nature of the Curse of Caine breaks the link with your avatar. Of course, with the new powers to steal avatars there may be a Discipline or spell that can rejoin you with your Phylactery, even if the link it's broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-19-2017, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T13:10:02-07:00","id":1105495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=1105456#post1105456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Shove your avatar into an object (creating a phylactery)<br /> 2) Get embraced<br /> 3) ...<br /> 4) Profit<br /> <br /> Edit: Im only joking, but i've seen worse things around my groups table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, I've mused in the past about a vampire antagonist that stole a mage's phylactery, and used it as an integral focus for Sphere magick. I don't think I would ever make it a thing a vampire could commonly pull off. Like, the one phylactery had this as a unique property. Hence why it's sought after by basically everyone who knows about it.<br /> <br /> Then again, I just kind of want an antagonist like <a href=\"https://youtu.be/B9za3TrVT3g\" target=\"_blank\">Dio Brando</a>. Not only a vampire, but also having cool magic powers. Stopping time all over the place, and generally being one of the most frightening villains around because of his stolen True Magick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T04:32:02-07:00","id":1105647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=1105493#post1105493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've heard of that reasoning before...and it has it's merit.<br /> <br /> One of the problems of undead in mage is the idea that the avatar leaves the body in the moment of death...but if your avatar it's trapped in an object, then it doesn't go away.<br /> <br /> This it's one of the ways the canon Lich rite (of Dead Magic) can be performed without needing Spirit. <br /> <br /> Of course, being vampire it's different from being a Lich, so the ST can easily say that the same principle doesn't apply because the nature of the Curse of Caine breaks the link with your avatar. Of course, with the new powers to steal avatars there may be a Discipline or spell that can rejoin you with your Phylactery, even if the link it's broken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dead Magic is not so fresh in my mind, but it strikes me as odd that you can shove your Avatar in an object without some knowledge of Spirit (4ish?).<br /> <br /> It is after all a form of Spirit","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T09:10:03-07:00","id":1106081,"title":"","content":"Yeah, to toss your avatar into an object you need Spirit for sure. In the Lich rote you create your Phylactery with Spirit 3-this is weird, I would think the level should be 4, at the very least, the level needed to create Fetishes.<br /> <br /> However, if you purchased the -7 points defect, then you already have your Avatar shoved into a Phylactery, and thus you shouldn't need Spirit at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T13:52:50-07:00","id":1106241,"title":"","content":"Spirit 3 I can live with, it isn't some Spirit it is your Avatar.<br /> Like in altering your personal pattern is Life 3 instead of 4.<br /> <br /> The Phylactery flaw comes quite in handy for would be liches.<br /> <br /> In my campaign I have a related issue.<br /> One player has inherited the Avatar from a Tremere, and she has traced him...(he took the Enemy flaw and specified it to represent a Tremere sorceress he loves and/or is blood bound to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T08:18:58-07:00","id":1106564,"title":"","content":"How does him loving or being blood bound translate into enemy? Is the Tremere trying to take him down?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13562-lordmagnusen","name":"lordmagnusen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T11:15:40-07:00","id":1106657,"title":"","content":"He loves her, not the other way round. The Tremere is interested with the Avatar of the Mage. And because of this she doesn't want to kill him (not until she gets \u201cher\u201c Avatar back).<br /> Likewise he wouldn't want to kill her either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T12:22:25-07:00","id":1106689,"title":"","content":"That still doesn't very much jive with using &quot;Enemy&quot;...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13562-lordmagnusen","name":"lordmagnusen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T23:01:34-07:00","id":1106897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lordmagnusen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=1106689#post1106689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That still doesn't very much jive with using &quot;Enemy&quot;...</div> </div> </div> </div>Adversary would be better, sure.<br /> <br /> I want to circumvent the stereotype of \u201cyour enemy wants you dead because of reasons\u201c.<br /> <br /> <br /> If Players of the campaign \u201cUlmer Geld\u201c stumble upon this post, don't read!<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Sophia Ovirstoth (the Tremere) is interested in Francesco di Palma (the PC) because he inherited the Avatar (a Sparrow) which Sophia lost due zo the embrace.<br /> <br /> If she would kill him, she has to trace the sparrow again, so she doesn't want to at the moment. If this wouldn't be an issue it would be detrimental for the game if Sophia has already found and reached Francesco. Because an Ancillae/Elder (haven't decided yet) would wipe the floor with an relatively fresh mage (60 XP above standard starting level).<br /> <br /> What things mages fear more than death? <br /> Gilgul<br /> Falling<br /> probably Madness<br /> <br /> If Sophia succeeds Francesco looses his Avatar or he is held captive untill she manages to snatch the Avatar from him.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12022,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","user":"Nonsense","date":".  spelling, more thoughts 06-23-2017, 02:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T06:37:18-07:00","id":1106993,"title":"","content":"Adversary sounds much better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13562-lordmagnusen","name":"lordmagnusen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T07:40:47-07:00","id":1107012,"title":"","content":"There are, indeed, many ways that an adversary can oppose or stymie a character.<br /> <br /> If the Tremere doesn't want the mage to die (yet), she may be inclined to act to prevent him from engaging in activities that might threaten his life...even if they are risks he wants to take. This might involve thwarting attempts by the mage to obtain weapons or armor, so he has a harder time initiating conflicts. It might involve strategically assassinating the mage's enemies, but in a way that causes more problems for the mage in the long run (the enemy's friends might come looking for revenge, or the enemy might have had information the mage can't get from their corpse, or the fact that the mage and his enemy were in opposition is public knowledge and it raises questions of foul play, etc). The Tremere could simply decide that, if the mage's freedom of movement is limited, he can't as easily get himself killed. So she tries to get him arrested (even house arrest could work), steals his car, gets his passport or Visa destroyed or revoked, or leaves him bedridden through magical sickness.<br /> <br /> On another note, if the Tremere wants to eventually get her Avatar back, it'll probably require some grand Ritual. Since the mage isn't going to be okay with this plan, she needs the ability to nab him at any time. Which will be difficult, since he's a mage and therefore categorically dangerous. The Tremere could oppose him, therefore, by attacking his continued ability to use magick effectively. Denying him access to rare and vital spell components. Breaking or stealing his wand or other Instruments. Raiding his Library of its important tomes (which would also benefit the Tremere, since she expects to regain her Awakened magick in the future). Killing his Familiar, if he has one; it'll hurt, definitely, but he'll survive, and the Familiar could be thorn in the Tremere's side when the capture needs to happen. Arranging the presence of Sleeper witnesses wherever the mage goes, so his hands become tied by fear of Paradox. Pillaging or cutting off his supply of Quintessence (probably Tass, since its more ephemeral manifestations are difficult for a vampire to find).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T00:38:21-07:00","id":1107248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=1107012#post1107012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are, indeed, many ways that an adversary can oppose or stymie a character.<br /> <br /> If the Tremere doesn't want the mage to die (yet), she may be inclined to act to prevent him from engaging in activities that might threaten his life...even if they are risks he wants to take. This might involve thwarting attempts by the mage to obtain weapons or armor, so he has a harder time initiating conflicts. It might involve strategically assassinating the mage's enemies, but in a way that causes more problems for the mage in the long run (the enemy's friends might come looking for revenge, or the enemy might have had information the mage can't get from their corpse, or the fact that the mage and his enemy were in opposition is public knowledge and it raises questions of foul play, etc). The Tremere could simply decide that, if the mage's freedom of movement is limited, he can't as easily get himself killed. So she tries to get him arrested (even house arrest could work), steals his car, gets his passport or Visa destroyed or revoked, or leaves him bedridden through magical sickness.<br /> <br /> On another note, if the Tremere wants to eventually get her Avatar back, it'll probably require some grand Ritual. Since the mage isn't going to be okay with this plan, she needs the ability to nab him at any time. Which will be difficult, since he's a mage and therefore categorically dangerous. The Tremere could oppose him, therefore, by attacking his continued ability to use magick effectively. Denying him access to rare and vital spell components. Breaking or stealing his wand or other Instruments. Raiding his Library of its important tomes (which would also benefit the Tremere, since she expects to regain her Awakened magick in the future). Killing his Familiar, if he has one; it'll hurt, definitely, but he'll survive, and the Familiar could be thorn in the Tremere's side when the capture needs to happen. Arranging the presence of Sleeper witnesses wherever the mage goes, so his hands become tied by fear of Paradox. Pillaging or cutting off his supply of Quintessence (probably Tass, since its more ephemeral manifestations are difficult for a vampire to find).</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> I want to add, that we play 1450 in Ulm, Germany.<br /> Some things are different but the general ideas are along the lines of what I have in stock for the future.<br /> <br /> The Tremere even helps out now and then, this leaves the player somewhat puzzled, questioning himself why she helps him without wanting something in return, or does she?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T08:58:16-07:00","id":1107332,"title":"","content":"Can't the Tremere make friends with the Mage who has her Avatar - which would be good for a spell and/or process that makes her human/True Mage again - and aim to get another Avatar / have another Avatar guided to her?<br /> The enemy Flaw of the Mage could then be exchanged for being enemies to Tradition Mages or Technocrats who would want to prevent this, for whatever reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T00:14:22-07:00","id":1107558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/101642-what-happens-when-a-kindred-attempts-to-embrace-a-mage?p=1107332#post1107332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't the Tremere make friends with the Mage who has her Avatar - which would be good for a spell and/or process that makes her human/True Mage again - and aim to get another Avatar / have another Avatar guided to her?<br /> The enemy Flaw of the Mage could then be exchanged for being enemies to Tradition Mages or Technocrats who would want to prevent this, for whatever reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a possibility, but as long as none of them believes that this is possible it isn't an option.<br /> <br /> That being said, the Tremere is trying to make a friendly (if one sided) relationship. This way it is easier to make use of the Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}